Attribution and inspiration (NO upstream code or weights are bundled)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

The CTM and GPM (Doc-to-LoRA) mechanism-aligned modules are inspired by the
following works from Sakana AI:
  - Continuous Thought Machines (CTM), Apache License 2.0
    https://github.com/SakanaAI/continuous-thought-machines
  - Doc-to-LoRA, Apache License 2.0
    https://github.com/SakanaAI/doc-to-lora

This repository does NOT redistribute their source code or model weights.
The optional adapter udos/adapters/sakana_ctm_adapter.py only fetches
upstream artifacts at runtime via huggingface_hub when you explicitly enable
it; the rest of the engine is a lightweight, CPU-runnable mechanism
alignment ("analogy, not reproduction").

The open-source resource catalog (udos/connectors/_catalog_data.py,
udos/connectors/registry_build.py, docs/opensource_catalog.*,
docs/third_party/*.md) contains only metadata, architecture notes and links
to third-party robot foundation models, datasets and simulators. No
third-party source code or pretrained weights are redistributed here. Each
such project and dataset remains governed by its own license, which is
recorded in the catalog entries; consult the upstream projects before any
commercial or model-weight use.

The model checkpoints under checkpoints/ are produced by this project's own
synthetic-dynamics training pipeline (a ~52k-parameter PhysicsPredictor).
They contain no third-party or upstream pretrained weights.

Fine-grained biophysical modules (udos/finesim, udos/dendrite) are CPU
reference implementations of published equations and mechanisms; they do
not run NEURON/CoreNEURON and do not reproduce the papers' effect sizes.
Citations are listed in the module docstrings and in docs/.
